{
  "_comment": [
    "Which chapter has to define each idea. `terms.py` gates Vulkan names; this gates",
    "the concepts and mathematics those names sit on top of, which no amount of API",
    "vocabulary teaches. A reader meeting 'the normal matrix' needs it derived, not",
    "mentioned.",
    "",
    "The check is that the concept appears in the chapter's `Words introduced in this",
    "chapter` table, because that table is where this series defines its terms.",
    "",
    "Two different jobs are being done here, and they are worth telling apart:",
    "",
    "  * Part 1's lists were read back out of the tables that already exist, so the gate",
    "    proves nothing about Part 1 that Part 1 did not already say. It is a ratchet:",
    "    it fails if a term is ever dropped from a table it currently sits in.",
    "",
    "  * Part 2 onward is curated before the article is written, from what the sample",
    "    and its shaders actually do. There the gate is a real check -- it fails until",
    "    the chapter defines what it uses.",
    "",
    "A concept is listed against the chapter that FIRST needs it. `specialisation",
    "constant` belongs to 1.9 even though 2.5 and 2.6 are what finally use it."
  ],
